<name>Wadi Ghadir EM survey plan</name><description>written by Mohamed Sobh, LIAG</description>
<Placemark><name>R1 (TEM central loop)</name><description>background resistivity and noise level: calibrates every other line</description><LineString><coordinates>34.908164,24.760101,0 34.918049,24.759975,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L2 (TEM + AMT)</name><description>strongest magnetic anomaly, dense and magnetic: possible active serpentinisation front (H2 source)</description><LineString><coordinates>34.742468,24.717944,0 34.756265,24.705015,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L1 (TEM + AMT)</name><description>shallow magnetic body with a dense and magnetic core: H2 source candidate</description><LineString><coordinates>34.779591,24.706129,0 34.796141,24.690609,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L4 (TEM + AMT)</name><description>deep magnetic body (top ~700 m) and its faults: source at depth and pathways</description><LineString><coordinates>34.888801,24.767887,0 34.896179,24.794118,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L5 (TEM central loop)</name><description>shallow magnetic body in the east: serpentinite or magnetite-rich mafic rock</description><LineString><coordinates>34.936281,24.783912,0 34.941891,24.766600,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L6 (TEM central loop)</name><description>low-density body at the coast: reservoir and seal side of the H2 system</description><LineString><coordinates>34.989000,24.824535,0 35.007879,24.829929,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>L3 (AMT)</name><description>deep dense block (top ~1.1 km): AMT only, fluid paths into it</description><LineString><coordinates>34.860271,24.748443,0 34.884207,24.777187,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
